title: Code lenses of an extension sit above their functions, run their command when clicked, follow edits and change when the extension says so
folders: rust-small
extensions: views-extension
expect-log: code lenses for main\.rs
expect-log: script: lenses of src/main\.rs line 4: ▸ Run \| 1 reference
expect-log: running the code lens '▸ Run'
expect-log: showing the uses of 'main'
expect-log: script: lenses of src/main\.rs line 4: ▸ Run \| 1 reference \| more
expect-log: script: lenses of src/main\.rs line 3: ▸ Run \| 1 reference
expect-file: rust-small/qa-ran.txt :: run main 3
expect-file: rust-small/qa-ran.txt :: more lenses true

wait 3000
goto src/main.rs
wait 2500
mark lenses
wait 600
lens report src/main.rs
lens src/main.rs 4 1
wait 800
lens src/main.rs 4 2
wait 2000
mark uses
wait 600
command qa.lenses.more
wait 2000
lens report src/main.rs
goto src/util.rs
wait 2500
mark first-line
wait 600
goto src/main.rs
wait 1500
edit src/main.rs 3 1
type fn extra() {}
wait 2500
lens report src/main.rs
mark edited
wait 600
key save
wait 800
quit
